# 📊 Credit Card Usage Segmentation (Capstone Project)

## 📌 Project Overview
This project aims to segment credit card customers based on their spending patterns and financial behavior.  
Using **EDA**, **Feature Engineering**, **PCA**, and **K-Means Clustering**, meaningful customer groups were created to help banks improve marketing strategies and customer understanding.

---

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies Used
- Python  
- Pandas, NumPy  
- Matplotlib, Seaborn  
- Scikit-Learn  
- PCA for dimensionality reduction  
- K-Means for clustering

---

## 🔍 Steps Performed in the Project

### **1. Data Preprocessing**
- Missing value handling  
- Outlier treatment (capping)  
- Feature scaling  

### **2. Feature Engineering**
- Credit Utilization Ratio  
- Payment behavior metrics  
- Spending pattern indicators  

### **3. Dimensionality Reduction (PCA)**
- Selected optimal number of components  
- Retained maximum variance  

### **4. Clustering**
- Applied K-Means  
- Used Elbow Method & Silhouette Score  
- Analyzed cluster behavior  

---

## 🎯 Business Insights
- Identify high-value customer groups  
- Create targeted marketing campaigns  
- Better credit limit allocation  
- Improve customer retention strategies  

